  "confidence": 0.94,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U4", "U24"],
      "pins": ["U4.4", "U4.5", "U24.4", "U24.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both isolated CAN transceivers have their primary-side GND1 and bus-side GND2 pins connected to the same GND net, bypassing the galvanic isolation barrier.",
      "expected": "For the specified isolated CAN buses, the transceiver-side grounds must remain separated across the isolation barrier; the bus-side ground should not be tied directly to primary GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U24\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U24\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces lose their intended galvanic isolation, allowing ground-potential differences and transients on the bus side to couple directly into the motherboard ground.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U13", "U16", "U18", "U26", "U28", "U33", "U45", "U46", "U47", "U48", "U50", "U52"],
      "pins": ["U13.1", "U16.1", "U18.1", "U26.1", "U28.1", "U33.1", "U45.1", "U46.1", "U47.1", "U48.1", "U50.1", "U52.1"],
      "nets": ["/NET0118", "NET0116", "NET0166", "NET0008", "NET0092"],
      "observed": "These parts are valued SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1, but their custom symbol assigns pin 1 the function /OE and the netlist connects pin 1 to control nets. The SN74LVC1G07 is an open-drain buffer whose pin 1 is not an output-enable pin. The component metadata instead lists an MPN for a different part, U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R.",
      "expected": "The fitted part and symbol/BOM identity should agree, and any pin used as /OE must be an actual output-enable pin. If the stated SN74LVC1G07 is fitted, pin 1 cannot provide the depicted enable function.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U13\")\n      (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"1\") (name \"/OE\") (type \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U13\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"/OE\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the valued SN74LVC1G07 is fitted, the connected control signals cannot enable or disable the buffers as represented, so functions that depend on those gates—including the described e-stop sink behavior—may not work as intended. The conflicting MPN makes the intended fitted device ambiguous.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist directly ties both grounds of each isolated CAN transceiver together, defeating the specified isolation. It also contains a buffer symbol/value/BOM mismatch: control nets use pin 1 as /OE on parts valued SN74LVC1G07, which has no such enable pin."
}

